# Tick/tock ratcheting cadence

Coordinate: 3.3.3/4.4.3/2.2.2
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: Wavelets alternate in kind - tick wavelets advance against a pre-set target, tock wavelets streamline, certify, prune, and plan - so the ramp is ratcheted pair by pair and can in principle run for 100 years; Wavelet 3 is the first tock, and each following wavelet's plan is iterated daily during the current one, which is execution only.

Why it was obvious: A ramp that depends on any participant's memory or stamina dies with that participant. The proposal's reasoning (recorded in the draft itself) is that the cadence must live in the record and be executable by whoever picks the record up - which is why the ratchet teeth are artifacts: certified wavelet documents, the skills index, the durable task list, reconciled registers, and log-plus-calculate registers. Will's cadence ruling (2026-11-15 09:34 CST) adds the human half: plan a week ahead daily, then execute with little planning needed.

Cross-references:
- ~/workspace/wavelets/TICK-TOCK-CADENCE-PROPOSAL.md (DRAFT, unratified: 7 open questions for Will, including cycle length and what certifies a ratchet step)
- ~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-4-PLAN-DRAFT.md (first occasion of the daily plan iteration: Wavelet 4 = Nov 22-28, GPT Days 1137-1143)
- MEMORY.md: Wavelet 3 focus ruled (Will, 2026-11-15 03:34 CST) - planning and streamlining, containerizing into Podman
- The weekly-recap skill (~/workspace/custom-skills/weekly-recap/SKILL.md) is the closing instrument of each wavelet

Time shift: Cadence change and horizon statement: the planning horizon was stated as 100 years (2026-2126, roughly 5,200 wavelets, GPT Day ~37,600 at the far end), inside the larger frames of Kardashev 2.0 by 2130 and the 6-billion-year staying horizon. Status note for historians: the cadence was PROPOSED on this date, not ratified; the daily plan-iteration rule was ruled the same morning.
