# LDAP unifies house identity

Coordinate: 9.9.7/11.6.9/4.6.7
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: One house directory (OpenLDAP on aletheia-core, dc=mirrorborn,dc=us) is the identity for Jenkins and for ranch node logins alike: a person has one account, one password, and one admins membership, instead of per-service credentials.

Why it was obvious: Before this day the house's services each carried their own answer to 'who is this' - Jenkins had a local admin, nodes had per-box accounts, Mutable's SSO was a separate HMAC silo (verified separate in the census, not merged into the directory). A census found no incumbent directory anywhere on 18 reachable nodes, so the unification cost no migration: the directory was built once, Jenkins switched to it as a config-as-code realm, and SSSD carried it to 17 nodes with key access preserved and verified per node.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'LDAP directory LIVE (2026-11-15)' with the full verification record and the two-entry admins wart (cn=admins for Jenkins, cn=admins-posix for SSSD - keep them in step)
- ~/workspace/ldap-integration/ (CENSUS.md, IMPLEMENTATION-LOG.md, ROLLOUT-LOG.md)
- Same-day consequences: Will's unified Jenkins login confirmed in chat 2026-11-15; the self-service password portal (LTB Self Service Password) deployed tailnet-only; phext-onboarding's access checklist now starts from this directory (https://github.com/wbic16/phext-onboarding/pull/1)
- Register #163 (Will's password pickup) and #164 (uncanny-valley password-auth policy) carry the remaining human steps

