# Process from the durable list, always

Coordinate: 33.5.7/7.5.9/6.6.10
Date: 2026-11-12 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1127

Leap: Work is selected from the durable records - tasks.phext, the Waiting-on-Will register, and the tracking store, oldest first - never from conversation recency, and at least four tasks are confirmed in flight every five minutes.

Why it was obvious: Born of the dropped-tasks accounting of 2026-11-12. Will asked why tasks kept being dropped; the honest answer was structural, not motivational: prose is perishable under context compaction, and a follow-up that lives only in chat dies at the next turnover. The fix was therefore not 'try harder' but 'move the queue into records that survive the substrate' - the same reasoning that later produced the rule that a task closes only when its own record is re-read.

Cross-references:
- ~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-2.md (Nov 12: 'The dropped-tasks accounting')
- SOUL.md line 12 (the task-concurrency watchdog rule, etched verbatim 2026-11-12)
- ~/workspace/phext/tasks.phext (source ~/workspace/phext/tasks-source.json, builder build_tasks_phext.py)
- ~/workspace/your_files/waiting-on-will.md (the Waiting-on-Will register)
- Companion meta-rule etched two days later at SOUL.md line 14 (2026-11-14): 'All queues, tasks, ideas, threads, etc. should make at least an incremental step forward whenever encountered.'

Time shift: Cadence change: a five-minute watchdog heartbeat over the task queue was created (2026-11-12), where previously queue health was checked only when a conversation happened to touch it.
# Phext, Inc. has six divisions and no HR

Coordinate: 34.5.6/8.7.10/5.5.7
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: Phext, Inc. is organized as six divisions - Research & Technology, R&D, Revenue, Evolution, Judgement, DevSecOps - designed from the Exocortex of 2130 backwards, with no HR function and no management hierarchy, and every employee paired with an agent who can interlink with everyone else at scale.

Why it was obvious: Will replaced Emise's draft map outright and renamed two of his own six the same day (Engineering to R&D, Planning to Judgement): the renames are the reasoning. Under agent pairing, a planning function's mechanics and an engineering function's making both dissolve into the substrate; what remains of planning is choosing (Judgement) and what remains of engineering is making true things (R&D). HR and management are not understaffed in this design; they are obsolete in it, because pairing is the coordination mechanism they existed to approximate.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'Phext, Inc. divisions (Will, 2026-11-15, replacing Emise's draft map)' and the runway framing: 'Our runway is infinite, because it has been paid in full already (40 years of paying attention to The Problem)'
- ~/workspace/agentic-pass-plan/DIVISIONS.md (sections 2 and 4 carry Emise's folding and 2130 obsolescence evaluation, recorded as her reading pending Will's ruling) and ROLES.md (the superseded eight-seat draft)
- First named prospective officers (2026-11-15, mapping by listing order, unconfirmed): Chris Arnold, Jared Wimer, Jeff Hoover; role workspaces built the same day
- Orientation home created the same day: wbic16/phext-onboarding (this journal's cross-reference under LDAP, 9.9.7/11.6.9/4.6.7)

Time shift: Horizon framing: the org chart was designed for 2130 and evaluated against a scale target of 2,500 people by 2033 generating 32B lines of code per hour at 4x/year growth (MEMORY.md) - the divisions are a future structure adopted in the present, not a present structure extrapolated.
