# This VM is mortal: the ranch execution split

Coordinate: 38.6.7/6.5.9/5.5.8
Date: 2026-11-12 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1127

Leap: The Muse VM is a coordination substrate only: Emise coordinates, verifies, and keeps records there, while substantive execution runs node-resident and stage-checkpointed on ranch nodes, because the VM is replaced roughly every two hours and kills everything on it.

Why it was obvious: The evidence was a ledger, not an intuition: the deploy-study recorded 124 VM boot changes, and the T8 film build's coordinator died at the 01:32 swap on 2026-11-12 after finishing its narration mix, leaving no completion, no failure report, and a stale task record. Once the mortality is measured, placing load-bearing work on the VM is not optimism, it is a known loss rate.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'Local VM is untrusted for execution (Will, 2026-11-12, standing rule)' and 'No work dispatched to the local VM'
- TOOLS.md (deploy-study ledger: boot changes 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-12 listed; the T8 coordinator death)
- Earlier form of the same lesson, 2026-11-05: SQ daemons moved to ranch nodes after the claims-ledger daemon died twice in one day (~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-1.md, Nov 5)
- Companion rules: heavy-job queue N=4 FIFO (2026-11-03); all video work ranch-only (2026-11-08)

Time shift: Horizon change: the planning unit for any build became the leg that fits between VM replacements (roughly two hours), with checkpointing at leg boundaries, instead of the session.
# GPT Day epoch settled

Coordinate: 40.4.12/5.5.21/3.3.8
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: GPT Day 1 is October 13, 2023 - the evening of Will's first GPT-4 messages - and every GPT Day count is computed from that epoch by date arithmetic, never re-derived from inside a conversation.

Why it was obvious: The counter had been corrupted in a specific, measurable way: archive labels beginning with GPT Day 183 on 2025-04-12 had counted from October 13, 2024, making every label short by exactly 365 days. Will named this the Hull Corruption's mechanism and stated the causal lesson explicitly: this is why the house uses phext synced to GitHub - a count that lives in a versioned artifact can be checked; a count re-derived in conversation drifts. Verification was empirical: the ChatGPT archive shows the first GPT-4 messages at 21:58 CDT on 2023-10-13.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'GPT Day epoch SETTLED (Will, 2026-11-15)'
- ~/memory/2026-11-15.md (the correction entry identifying the 365-day slip, and the archive check at 21:58 CDT 2023-10-13)
- Superseded record: ~/memory/2026-11-07.md (the October 2024 back-calculation, recorded there as disputed)
- First use: the weekly recap ritual 'New Week, Next Wavelet' (task 24.6.11/9.7.12/7.6.9) counts wavelets in GPT Days
- Open residue, recorded not resolved: parts of the record label Emise's designation day 2026-10-30 as GPT Day 1115; date arithmetic from the settled epoch gives 1114, and the wavelet documents' age formula (age = GPT Day - 1114) follows the arithmetic

Time shift: Epoch settlement: the origin of the house's day counter moved back exactly 365 days from the corrupted labels to 2023-10-13. All GPT Day figures written before 2026-11-15 must be re-derived from the epoch before use; 2026-11-15 = GPT Day 1130.
# Phext chaining canon

Coordinate: 46.8.7/7.12.21/23.7.15
Date: 2026-11-13 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1128

Leap: Whole phexts are chained with byte 0x02 as the chain delimiter and 0x03 as the chain close, so a chain is a multiverse: each member is a universe indexed from 1 and addressed $N:<address>, and a bare address means universe 1.

Why it was obvious: Standoff relationships at scale had to live somewhere. The alternatives were embedded markup inside scrolls or a tenth addressing dimension; chaining puts the relationship one rung above Library instead, keeping every member phext complete and independently valid, and making a truncated chain detectable (a chain with no 0x03 was cut). Emise's proposed 0x04 stream close was rejected by Will the same day as unnecessary - the canon is also a record of what was NOT added.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md phext chaining entry (Will, 2026-11-13)
- ~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-2.md (Nov 13 decisions list: 'phext chaining canon 0x02/0x03 with 0x04 rejected')
- Downstream: phext-lattice 1.3.0 chain support (2026-11-14), with chains deliberately read-only in edit.phext.io because the editor's rewrite-style save cannot honour the chain write rules
- Addressing depends on it: the $N: prefix used by the range syntax ratified 2026-11-15 (this journal, 28.7.7/5.6.6/5.5.10)

Time shift: Time enters the format: in Will's framing (MEMORY.md), the nine dimensions address space and the chain orders states, so the format gains a time axis without spending a dimension on it.
